1 EOD
    In a command procedure, the DECK command makes the lines after it
    data, for the image reading the procedure's input (SYS$INPUT), even
    when they start with "$".  The data ends at an EOD command, or, with
    /DOLLARS, at a line starting with the string given; after that, any
    "$" line ends data again.  DECK comes after the command that runs
    the image, where its data begins.

    Syntax:

        DECK [/DOLLARS[=string]]
        EOD

    The string is 1 to 15 characters, uppercased unless quoted, and ends
    the data at a line starting with it, case and all.  An image reading
    an EOD line comes to its end of file there, and the next read gets
    the data after it.  DECK read as a command, with no image reading,
    is DCL-W-IVVALU, and EOD that no image reads does nothing.

    Example:

        $ TYPE SYS$INPUT
        $ DECK
        $ This line starts with a dollar sign, and is typed.
        $ EOD
